questions.solution:
(A) $1^{{}^{\circ}}$ amines give a bad smelling compound, called carbylamine, with alcoholic $\mathrm{KOH}$ and $\mathrm{CHCl}_3$. The reaction is called carbylamine reaction.

\begin{aligned}$ \mathrm{CH}}_{3}  \mathrm{CH}$}_{2} $\mathrm{CH}}_{2}  \mathrm{CH}$}_{2} $\mathrm{NH}}_{2} \stackrel{ \mathrm{CHCl}$}_{3}+$\text{ alc } \mathrm{KOH}$}{\longrightarrow} \\
 $\mathrm{CH}}_{3}\left(\mathrm{CH}$}_{2}\right)_3 $\mathrm{NC}\\
 \text{ bad smelling }\\
&
\end{aligned}

(B) Terminal alkynes like \mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{C} \equiv \mathrm{CH}$ give white precipitate with ammoniacal $\mathrm{AgNO}_3$.

\begin{array}{r}$\mathrm{CH}}_{3}  \mathrm{C} \equiv \mathrm{CH}+\mathrm{AgNO}$}_{3}+$\mathrm{NH}}_{4}  \mathrm{OH} \longrightarrow\\
\mathrm{CH}$}_{3} $\mathrm{C} \equiv \mathrm{CAg}\\
\text{ white ppt }
\end{array}

(C) Ester \left(\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{CH}_2 \mathrm{COOCH}_3\right)$ undergoes alkaline hydrolysis.

\begin{array}{r}$\mathrm{CH}}_{3}  \mathrm{CH}$}_{2} $\mathrm{COOCH}}_{3}+ \mathrm{NaOH} \longrightarrow\\
\mathrm{CH}$}_{3} $\mathrm{CH}}_{2}  \mathrm{COONa}+\mathrm{CH}$}_{3} $\mathrm{OH}
\end{array}

(D) $2^{{}^{\circ}}$ alcohols (the alcohols that have \mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{CHOH}$ - group) give cloudiness with Lucas reagent (anhy $\mathrm{ZnCl}_2+$ conc $\mathrm{HCl}$ ) within 5 minutes.
